SUMMARY:The Music Man
DESCRIPTION:Seventy-six trombones. One unforgettable musical!\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				Meredith Willson’s six-time Tony Award®-winning beloved musical comedy The Music Man marches into Houston with laughter\, heart\, and all the music you love. Following the fast-talking traveling salesman Harold Hill as he cons the people of River City\, Iowa\, into buying instruments and uniforms for a boys’ band that he vows to organize. Featuring songs such as “Seventy-Six Trombones\,” “Trouble\,” “’Till There Was You\,” “Pick-a-Little\,” and “Gary\, Indiana\,” The Music Man is a classic musical to be shared with every generation. \n			\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n			\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n			\n				\n				\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				CRITICAL ACCLAIM FOR THE MUSIC MAN\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n					\n			\n			\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n					\n			\n			\n			\n					– The Telegraph \n					\n					“A joyous\, blissful Broadway event!” \n					\n				\n				\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n					\n			\n			\n			\n					– Variety \n					\n					“Grand and Glorious!” “…totally enchanting abso-tootin’-lutely smashing revival. It will give you new life.” \n					\n				\n				\n			\n			\n				\n			\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n			\n				\n				\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				PERFORMANCE SCHEDULE\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n					\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				Tuesday\, Sept 15\, 7:30 p.m. – H-E-B Community Night\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				Wednesday\, Sept 16\, 7:30 p.m. \n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				Thursday\, Sept 17\, 7:30 p.m. \n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				Friday\, Sept 18\, 8 p.m. — Post-Show Talkback with the Cast\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				Saturday\, Sept 19\, 2 p.m. \n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				Saturday\, Sept 19\, 8 p.m.\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				Sunday\, Sept 20\, 2 p.m. \n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				Sunday\, Sept 20\, 7:30 p.m. \n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				Tuesday\, Sept 22\, 7:30 p.m. \n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				Wednesday\, Sept 23\, 7:30 p.m. \n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				Thursday\, Sept 24\, 7:30 p.m. \n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				Friday\, Sept 25\, 8 p.m. \n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				Saturday\, Sept 26\, 2 p.m. — Open Captioned \n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				Saturday\, Sept 26\, 8 p.m. \n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				Sunday\, Sept 27\, 2 p.m. — ASL & Audio Described \n			\n				\n			\n				SUBSCRIBE NOW\n			\n				GET TICKETS!\n			\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				TICKETING INFO\nSeason tickets are available. 6-show packages start at just $34 per-show. \nTickets are $46 and are available online or by calling TUTS Guest Services at 713-558-8887. Tickets will also available in person Monday through Friday from Noon to 6 p.m. at the TUTS Box Office\, located in the Hobby Center lobby. \nDiscounted group tickets are available for parties of 10 or more.Theatre Under The Stars has a variety of accessibility options for guests.Learn more about accessible performances and other services here. \nRush tickets will be available for $35 at the box office for mezzanine and gallery seating starting 2 hours prior to curtain. \nQuestions about parking\, dining or other aspects of attending a TUTS show? We’ve got answers! \n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				RUN TIME\n2 hours and 30 minutes including intermission\n			\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n			\n				\n				\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				Photos\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n					\n                \n                    \n                        \n                            \n                            \