SUMMARY:Oh\, Mary!
DESCRIPTION:History has never been this unhinged.\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				Oh\, Mary! is a dark comedy about a miserable\, suffocated Mary Todd Lincoln in the weeks leading up to Abraham Lincoln’s assassination. Unrequited yearning\, alcoholism\, and suppressed desires abound in this 80-minute one-act play that finally examines the forgotten life and dreams of Mrs. Lincoln\, through the lens of an idiot (playwright Cole Escola). \nDeclared “one of the best comedies in years” by The New York Times\, Oh\, Mary! received two Tony Awards® including Best Direction of a Play (Sam Pinkleton)\, Drama League Awards for Outstanding Play and Outstanding Direction of a Play\, as well as a special citation from the New York Drama Critics’ Circle. It was named a finalist for the Pulitzer Prize for Drama. \n			\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				Cole Escola in Oh\, Mary! on Broadway. Photo by Emilio Madrid. \n			\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n			\n				\n				\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				CRITICAL ACCLAIM FOR OH\, MARY!\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n					\n			\n			\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n					\n			\n			\n			\n					—The New York Times\, Critic’s Pick\n					\n					“You’ll be losing your mind with joy.” \n					\n				\n				\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n					\n			\n			\n			\n					—The Hollywood Reporter\n					\n					“80 minutes of almost uninterrupted laughter. A work of genius.” \n					\n				\n				\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n					\n			\n			\n			\n					—Deadline\n					\n					“There’s funny\, there’s very funny\, and then there’s Oh\, Mary!” \n					\n				\n				\n			\n			\n				\n			\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n			\n				\n				\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				PERFORMANCE SCHEDULE\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n					\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				Tuesday\, April 27\, 7:30 p.m. – H-E-B Community Night\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				Wednesday\, April 28\, 7:30 p.m. \n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				Thursday\, April 29\, 7:30 p.m. — Out@TUTS Afterparty\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				Friday\, April 30\, 8 p.m. — Post-Show Talkback with the Cast\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				Saturday\, May 1\, 2 p.m. \n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				Saturday\, May 1\, 8 p.m. \n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				Sunday\, May 2\, 2 p.m. \n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				Sunday\, May 2\, 7:30 p.m. \n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				Tuesday\, May 4\, 7:30 p.m. \n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				Wednesday\, May 5\, 7:30 p.m. \n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				Thursday\, May 6\, 7:30 p.m. \n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				Friday\, May 7\, 8 p.m. \n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				Saturday\, May 8\, 2 p.m. — Open Captioned \n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				Saturday\, May 8\, 8 p.m. \n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				Sunday\, May 9\, 2 p.m. — ASL & Audio Described \n			\n				\n			\n				SUBSCRIBE NOW\n			\n				GET TICKETS!\n			\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				TICKETING INFO\nSeason tickets are available. 6-show packages start at just $34 per-show. \nTickets are $46 and are available online or by calling TUTS Guest Services at 713-558-8887. Tickets will also available in person Monday through Friday from Noon to 6 p.m. at the TUTS Box Office\, located in the Hobby Center lobby. \nDiscounted group tickets are available for parties of 10 or more.Theatre Under The Stars has a variety of accessibility options for guests.Learn more about accessible performances and other services here. \nRush tickets will be available for $35 at the box office for mezzanine and gallery seating starting 2 hours prior to curtain. \nQuestions about parking\, dining or other aspects of attending a TUTS show? We’ve got answers! \n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				RUN TIME\n1 hour and 20 minutes\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				CONTENT NOTICE\nOh\, Mary! contains explicit language\, adult themes and comedic material intended for mature audiences. This production features water-based haze and one single gunshot. \n			\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n			\n				\n				\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				Photos\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n					\n                \n                    \n                        \n                            \n                            \n                        \n                    \n                \n                    \n                        \n                            \n                            \n                        \n                    \n                \n                    \n                        \n                            \n                            \n                        \n                    \n                \n                    \n                        \n                            \n                            \n                        \n                    \n                \n                    \n                        \n                            \n                            \n                        \n                    \n                \n                    \n                        \n                            \n                            \n                        \n                    \n                \n                    \n                        \n                            \n                            \n                        \n                    \n                \n             \n				\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				Emilio Madrid\n			\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n			\n				\n				\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				VIDEOS\n			